We define a tool dependency graph (TDG) for each scenario G = (V, E), where nodes represent tools V and edges E capture the dependencies between them. The dependency structure is inferred with the help of an LLM based on two key principles:

(1) an edge is established from tool T A to tool T B if the output of T A is required as an input for T B ;

(2) an edge is drawn from T A to B if T B can only be invoked after T A in the logical sequence of the scenario. The resulting graph, G, serves as the foundational structure for reasoning, where paths represent valid sequences of tool invocations with contextual dependencies.

